Privacy Policy

This Privacy Policy describes how Multi Counter App (“the App”) handles user information.

1. Information Collection and Use

Multi Counter App does not require any user registration or login process.

The App:

Does not collect personal data

Does not request or store information such as name, email address, phone number, or user identifiers

Does not access device features such as location, contacts, camera, or microphone

2. Automatically Collected Information

The App itself does not collect or track any information that can identify users.

However, the Android operating system or Google Play Services may automatically collect anonymous technical data, such as:

Device model

Android version

App crash reports

This information is used solely to improve app stability and performance and does not include personally identifiable information.

3. Third-Party Services

Multi Counter App may rely on the following third-party services:

Google Play Services

These services operate under their own privacy policies. The App developer does not receive or store any personally identifiable data from these services.

4. Data Sharing

Since Multi Counter App does not collect personal data:

No data is shared with third parties

No data is sold, transferred, or disclosed

5. Data Security

Because no personal data is collected or stored within the App, there is no risk of personal data breaches from the App itself.

6. Children’s Privacy

Multi Counter App does not knowingly collect any personal information from children under the age of 13. The App is designed to function without collecting any user data.

7. Changes to This Privacy Policy

This Privacy Policy may be updated from time to time. Any changes will be reflected on this page.

